  "system": {
    "role": "caster",
    "tier": 1,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>The endpoint of a life consumed by materialism: the physical shell of a person whose soul faded from neglect, leaving only a mindless echo driven by the base impulse to acquire and possess. Husks shamble through the ruins of opulent pre-Disaster places, still going through the motions of their former lives, hands locked in a death grip around one meaningless object — a shattered smartphone, a tarnished medal.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Nahemoth, the Whispering Ones — the Hull of Malkuth. The Kingdom with the spirit gone: matter, inertia, and grip.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'You cannot have the thing it is holding. Nobody can. That is the whole tragedy, and also the treasure policy.'</em></p>",
